    {
      "text": "For an ideally banked curve, the expression for the angle is $\\tan \\theta = \\frac{v^2}{rg}$ or $\\theta = \\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{v^2}{rg}\\right)$, where $v$ is the speed, $r$ is the radius, and $g$ is the acceleration due to gravity.",
      "sources": [
        "S4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Rearranging this expression shows that the ideal speed $v$ depends on the radius of the curve $r$, the banking angle $\\theta$, and acceleration due to gravity $g$, and does not depend on the mass of the vehicle.",
